recommend keep-going -- harness_unresolved reads 10 and the roster scan's own ceiling is 10, so every assembled shape this tree holds sits at the boundary of what either instrument can read; six of the ten are roster guards covered by their own witnesses and four are pens that build a corpus at runtime, which means the honest next lap is not lowering that ceiling but naming which of the ten could ever hide a real program. The ruling still Keaton's from my last lap: which metric Comlink actually routes on.
